# Phase 10: LLM Gateway & AI Reasoning Layer

## Objective

Introduce the LLM as the reasoning layer.

The LLM receives **filtered, validated Uthenga data**, not raw database access.

## Architecture

```text
User Request
      ↓
TIE
      ↓
Retrieve
      ↓
Filter
      ↓
Rank
      ↓
Build Context
      ↓
LLM Gateway
      ↓
Structured Response
```

## LLM Gateway responsibilities

* Provider abstraction
* Model selection
* Structured output
* Prompt management
* Retry
* Timeout handling
* Rate limiting
* Token tracking
* Cost tracking
* Provider fallback

## Initial model providers

Keep the architecture provider-agnostic.

Potential providers:

* OpenAI
* Anthropic
* Gemini
* Other compatible providers
* Local models later

## Deliverables

* LLM Gateway
* Prompt infrastructure
* Structured output schemas
* Model configuration
* AI error handling

## Gate

TIE can send a validated travel context to an LLM and receive a predictable structured response.

