# Recommended MVP Boundary

There is a temptation here to build the entire spaceship immediately. I would resist it.

The first meaningful milestone should be:

```text
                 Uthenga
                    │
                    ▼
              Trip Planner
                    │
                    ▼
            User Travel Intent
                    │
                    ▼
             Context Engine
                    │
                    ▼
         Uthenga Vendor Retrieval
                    │
                    ▼
           Availability Filtering
                    │
                    ▼
             Ranking + Budget
                    │
                    ▼
                LLM Gateway
                    │
                    ▼
            Structured Itinerary
                    │
                    ▼
              Response Validator
                    │
                    ▼
          Bookable Recommendations
```

That is the **TIE MVP**.

Once that works reliably, we bolt on:

```text
MVP
 ↓
Google Maps
 ↓
Live Location
 ↓
Journey Simulation
 ↓
Live Journey
 ↓
Notifications
 ↓
Conversation
 ↓
Personalization
 ↓
Advanced ML
```

This gives the implementation agent a very clear marching order: **first make Uthenga intelligent, then make it location-aware, then make it live, then make it proactive, and only much later make it predictive with custom ML.**
